    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5790542656,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-284c349c179f",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 3620.3410539776296,
      "y": -2378.8492031795427,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 658.3486328125,
      "height": 192.5,
      "seed": 931371,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Target\nA target is the active warehouse execution context exposed to dbt and Jinja. In Core it is a named output\ninside `profiles.yml`; in the dbt platform it is assembled from environment, connection, credential,\nextended-attribute, and job or developer settings.\n\nIn Core, the profile can define `dev`, `ci`, and `prod` outputs; `--target prod` chooses the production output,\nwhile no flag falls back to the profile's default `target`.\n\nIn the dbt platform, `target` still exists in Jinja, but it is populated from platform settings. Orchestrator jobs\ndefine `target.name` per job and get other target attributes from the deployment connection; Studio IDE\ngets target values from the developer's connection and credentials.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-284c349c179f",
      "originalText": "Target\nA target is the active warehouse execution context exposed to dbt and Jinja. In Core it is a named output inside `profiles.yml`; in the dbt platform it is assembled from environment, connection, credential, extended-attribute, and job or developer settings.\n\nIn Core, the profile can define `dev`, `ci`, and `prod` outputs; `--target prod` chooses the production output, while no flag falls back to the profile's default `target`.\n\nIn the dbt platform, `target` still exists in Jinja, but it is populated from platform settings. Orchestrator jobs define `target.name` per job and get other target attributes from the deployment connection; Studio IDE gets target values from the developer's connection and credentials.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-target"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
