    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6542216454,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-6132240b1deb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 2904.969616200805,
      "y": -2145.341927528294,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 666.1689453125,
      "height": 192.5,
      "seed": 133507,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Runtime Paths\nRuntime paths tell dbt where to read support files and where to write command outputs. They matter\nbecause state comparison, deferral, docs, and observability depend on reading the right artifacts.\n\nIn Core, profiles directory defaults to the local profiles location unless `--profiles-dir` or\n`DBT_PROFILES_DIR` overrides it; `target-path` defaults to `target/`; `packages-install-path` defaults to\n`dbt_packages/`; logs default to a log path under the active project.\n\nIn the dbt platform, jobs run in managed execution infrastructure. The platform prepares the run\nenvironment, clones the configured code version, connects to the data platform, runs built-in and configured\ncommands, and surfaces logs, run steps, timings, and artifacts in the job run UI.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-6132240b1deb",
      "originalText": "Runtime Paths\nRuntime paths tell dbt where to read support files and where to write command outputs. They matter because state comparison, deferral, docs, and observability depend on reading the right artifacts.\n\nIn Core, profiles directory defaults to the local profiles location unless `--profiles-dir` or `DBT_PROFILES_DIR` overrides it; `target-path` defaults to `target/`; `packages-install-path` defaults to `dbt_packages/`; logs default to a log path under the active project.\n\nIn the dbt platform, jobs run in managed execution infrastructure. The platform prepares the run environment, clones the configured code version, connects to the data platform, runs built-in and configured commands, and surfaces logs, run steps, timings, and artifacts in the job run UI.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-runtime-paths"
      }
    },
    {
