      "width": 575.080078125,
      "height": 140.0,
      "seed": 643032,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Model And Property Files\nModel files contain executable model logic, while property files attach metadata to resources.\nThis split lets SQL stay focused on transformation and YAML carry docs, tests, contracts,\nsources, and versions.\n\nExample: `models/marts/orders.sql` defines a model; `models/marts/orders.yml` can define\n`description`, `columns`, `data_tests`, and `versions` for that model. A `sources:` block in a\nYAML file under `model-paths` declares external inputs.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-a72a551f6d3d",
      "originalText": "Model And Property Files\nModel files contain executable model logic, while property files attach metadata to resources. This split lets SQL stay focused on transformation and YAML carry docs, tests, contracts, sources, and versions.\n\nExample: `models/marts/orders.sql` defines a model; `models/marts/orders.yml` can define `description`, `columns`, `data_tests`, and `versions` for that model. A `sources:` block in a YAML file under `model-paths` declares external inputs.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-model-and-property-files"
      }
    },
