      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Parser Cache\nThe parser cache lets dbt reuse parse results when files and relevant context have not\nchanged. It exists to make large projects faster during repeated local and CI invocations.\n\nIn Core, the cache is commonly stored as `target/partial_parse.msgpack` in the local project\noutput path. In the dbt platform, parse caching is affected by the managed run environment,\ndbt version or engine, code version, environment settings, and available platform metadata.\n\nChanges to dbt version, installed packages, project config, profile-sensitive inputs, or parse-\nrelevant environment variables can invalidate enough context that dbt must re-parse more\nbroadly.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-2c3dbe517923",
      "originalText": "Parser Cache\nThe parser cache lets dbt reuse parse results when files and relevant context have not changed. It exists to make large projects faster during repeated local and CI invocations.\n\nIn Core, the cache is commonly stored as `target/partial_parse.msgpack` in the local project output path. In the dbt platform, parse caching is affected by the managed run environment, dbt version or engine, code version, environment settings, and available platform metadata.\n\nChanges to dbt version, installed packages, project config, profile-sensitive inputs, or parse-relevant environment variables can invalidate enough context that dbt must re-parse more broadly.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-parser-cache"
      }
    },
