      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Resource Identity\nResource identity is the stable name dbt uses after parsing. It is what\nselectors, artifacts, lineage, tests, and docs join on.\n\nExamples: a model can become `model.analytics.orders`; a source table\ncan become `source.analytics.stripe.payments`; a generic test becomes\nits own test node tied to the resources it checks.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d65fef93db09",
      "originalText": "Resource Identity\nResource identity is the stable name dbt uses after parsing. It is what selectors, artifacts, lineage, tests, and docs join on.\n\nExamples: a model can become `model.analytics.orders`; a source table can become `source.analytics.stripe.payments`; a generic test becomes its own test node tied to the resources it checks.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-resource-identity"
      }
    },
