    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7700746365,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-791e0996ae30",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1789.3646960136546,
      "y": -1199.2444169022965,
      "strokeColor": "#1F2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 536.18017578125,
      "height": 178.75,
      "seed": 673086,
      "groupIds": [
        "lge0hos9"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Extract Dependencies\nInfer graph edges from dbt-aware declarations, not from arbitrary SQL text. dbt looks inside\nparse-time Jinja and YAML structures for `ref()`, `source()`, `config()`, generic and singular\ntests, exposures, metrics, semantic models, saved queries, and docs references.\n\n`ref()` looks up a model, seed, or snapshot by name, optional package or project namespace,\nand optional version, then creates a dependency and later compiles to a relation. `source()`\nlooks up a declared `sources:` entry by source name and table name, then creates a\ndependency and later compiles to the declared database, schema, and identifier. Raw\n`database.schema.table` strings, dynamic SQL that hides the target from parsing, and\nwarehouse objects not declared as dbt resources do not create reliable dbt lineage.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-791e0996ae30",
      "originalText": "Extract Dependencies\nInfer graph edges from dbt-aware declarations, not from arbitrary SQL text. dbt looks inside parse-time Jinja and YAML structures for `ref()`, `source()`, `config()`, generic and singular tests, exposures, metrics, semantic models, saved queries, and docs references.\n\n`ref()` looks up a model, seed, or snapshot by name, optional package or project namespace, and optional version, then creates a dependency and later compiles to a relation. `source()` looks up a declared `sources:` entry by source name and table name, then creates a dependency and later compiles to the declared database, schema, and identifier. Raw `database.schema.table` strings, dynamic SQL that hides the target from parsing, and warehouse objects not declared as dbt resources do not create reliable dbt lineage.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-extract-dependencies"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4627331235,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-83a9a989bccd",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
