    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6505882639,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-a70bd211947e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1795.0538126967183,
      "y": -488.7755490992938,
      "strokeColor": "#1F2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 534.9677734375,
      "height": 195.0,
      "seed": 213981,
      "groupIds": [
        "lge0hos9"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Apply Selection Policy\nStart from the full manifest, then narrow it to the command's active work set. dbt reads CLI `--\nselect` and `--exclude`, selector definitions, graph operators such as `+`, set operators,\nselector methods such as `tag:`, `path:`, `source:`, `config:`, `state:`, and command-specific\nresource-type rules.\n\nSelection order is match methods first, then graph expansion, then set operations and\nexclusions, then final filtering by command type. For example, `dbt run` keeps runnable\nmodels after selection, while `dbt test` keeps tests; tests can also be selected indirectly\nthrough selected parents according to indirect-selection policy. State selectors read a\ncomparison manifest from `--state`; deferral reads a prior manifest from `--state` or `--defer-\nstate` and resolves unbuilt upstream refs to relations described there.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-a70bd211947e",
      "originalText": "Apply Selection Policy\nStart from the full manifest, then narrow it to the command's active work set. dbt reads CLI `--select` and `--exclude`, selector definitions, graph operators such as `+`, set operators, selector methods such as `tag:`, `path:`, `source:`, `config:`, `state:`, and command-specific resource-type rules.\n\nSelection order is match methods first, then graph expansion, then set operations and exclusions, then final filtering by command type. For example, `dbt run` keeps runnable models after selection, while `dbt test` keeps tests; tests can also be selected indirectly through selected parents according to indirect-selection policy. State selectors read a comparison manifest from `--state`; deferral reads a prior manifest from `--state` or `--defer-state` and resolves unbuilt upstream refs to relations described there.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-apply-selection"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9609069980,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-dc82451ce23b",
