    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8244654939,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-202a3ce32ed1",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1772.2620998609013,
      "y": -45.70536971979186,
      "strokeColor": "#1F2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 600.4501953125,
      "height": 178.75,
      "seed": 299932,
      "groupIds": [
        "lge0hos9"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Compile Selected Nodes\nRender selected resources using the active Jinja context: `target`, `var()`, `env_var()`, `this`, `model`,\n`graph`, adapter macros, package macros, dispatch rules, and command flags. Macro lookup uses\nnamespace and dispatch search order, so root-project macros and configured dispatch can override\npackage or adapter behavior.\n\n`ref()` resolves to the selected or deferred relation for the referenced model, seed, or snapshot;\n`source()` resolves to the declared source database, schema, and identifier; `this` resolves to the current\nnode's target relation after database, schema, alias, quoting, custom schema macros, and adapter rules\nare applied. The output is compiled SQL or executable materialization logic under the target path, while\nonly executed nodes usually receive full compiled execution details in artifacts.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-202a3ce32ed1",
      "originalText": "Compile Selected Nodes\nRender selected resources using the active Jinja context: `target`, `var()`, `env_var()`, `this`, `model`, `graph`, adapter macros, package macros, dispatch rules, and command flags. Macro lookup uses namespace and dispatch search order, so root-project macros and configured dispatch can override package or adapter behavior.\n\n`ref()` resolves to the selected or deferred relation for the referenced model, seed, or snapshot; `source()` resolves to the declared source database, schema, and identifier; `this` resolves to the current node's target relation after database, schema, alias, quoting, custom schema macros, and adapter rules are applied. The output is compiled SQL or executable materialization logic under the target path, while only executed nodes usually receive full compiled execution details in artifacts.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-compile-selected"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5792136078,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-335862c613a8",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 3022.04309501716,
      "y": -134.8333785892769,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 552.6967772011992,
      "height": 203.0,
      "seed": 589240,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
