    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9300251085,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-b3b1e49ae723",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 2835.701688004352,
      "y": 560.0970172456772,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 482.48046875,
      "height": 122.5,
      "seed": 931994,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Threads And Parallelism\nThreads control how many dbt tasks can be in flight, but they do not override\ndependency order or warehouse limits. More threads help only when the DAG\nhas enough independent work and the warehouse can handle it.\n\nExample: `threads: 8` can run eight independent models concurrently, but a\nnarrow chain of dependent models still runs mostly one at a time.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-b3b1e49ae723",
      "originalText": "Threads And Parallelism\nThreads control how many dbt tasks can be in flight, but they do not override dependency order or warehouse limits. More threads help only when the DAG has enough independent work and the warehouse can handle it.\n\nExample: `threads: 8` can run eight independent models concurrently, but a narrow chain of dependent models still runs mostly one at a time.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-threads-parallelism"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4803062764,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-16fc8ae48d0c",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
