      "width": 466.1220703125,
      "height": 157.5,
      "seed": 718968,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Platform Job Run\nA dbt platform job is more than a single local command. The platform\nprepares managed infrastructure, reclones the repository, connects to the\ndata platform, automatically includes `dbt deps`, then chains the configured\ncommands as run steps.\n\nExample: a deployment job can run source freshness first, then `dbt build --\nselect tag:hourly`, then docs generation. If a chained run step fails, later\ncommands normally do not run and the job ends with an error status.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-0f48be6bf566",
      "originalText": "Platform Job Run\nA dbt platform job is more than a single local command. The platform prepares managed infrastructure, reclones the repository, connects to the data platform, automatically includes `dbt deps`, then chains the configured commands as run steps.\n\nExample: a deployment job can run source freshness first, then `dbt build --select tag:hourly`, then docs generation. If a chained run step fails, later commands normally do not run and the job ends with an error status.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-platform-job-run"
      }
    },
