      "width": 499.5498046875,
      "height": 140.0,
      "seed": 484788,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Target Path\nTarget path is the output directory for dbt artifacts and compiled files. It matters\nbecause many later commands read artifacts from this directory.\n\nIn Core, default `target/` contains `manifest.json` and `run_results.json`; CI might\nuse `--target-path target/ci` so local artifacts do not overwrite CI state. In the dbt\nplatform, users usually reason about artifacts through run records and\nenvironment metadata rather than by manually managing a local target directory.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-e2b2d0eb9823",
      "originalText": "Target Path\nTarget path is the output directory for dbt artifacts and compiled files. It matters because many later commands read artifacts from this directory.\n\nIn Core, default `target/` contains `manifest.json` and `run_results.json`; CI might use `--target-path target/ci` so local artifacts do not overwrite CI state. In the dbt platform, users usually reason about artifacts through run records and environment metadata rather than by manually managing a local target directory.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "dbt-lifecycle-target-path"
      }
    },
